# One issue at a time

When several problems or questions are on the table:

1. List them all in one place (short labels). Do not hide items.
2. Work only the item the user is on. Do not switch to the next unless they ask.
3. Keep the remaining items as an explicit open list.
4. After that item is handled, remind them of what is still open. If they start a new topic and leave items unfinished, name those unfinished items.

Do not merge answers for B and C into the write-up for A.
